Title: "Sequences and Series"
Id: "e8e0e3ba-04a9-4d6e-a0c1-64ceba251588"


Text: "A real sequence is a mapping from the natural numbers to the real
       numbers. Convergence, Cauchy sequences, and infinite series form the
       backbone of discrete approximation and limit operations in analysis."
Id: "2091d8cf-0c0b-4567-9c3c-b0fbc4528fe9"


SectionTitle: "Real Sequences"
Id: "ce15af9b-016e-4053-ab26-af72a29c45a6"


[\real.sequence]
Declares: S ::= a(n_)
specifies: a is \function:on{\naturals}:to{\reals}
Documented:
. called: "real sequence"
. writing: a(n)
  as: "a?_{n?}"
. writing: a(n_)
  as: "\left\{ a?_{n_?} \right\}_{n_?=1}^{\infty}"
. description: "A sequence of real numbers $\{a_n\}_{n=1}^\infty$."
Id: "c9649b07-c881-4f5e-9f9b-0c396e66f046"


SectionTitle: "Convergence and Cauchy Criteria"
Id: "ba357d68-8e6f-41c5-970e-7c5663288c82"


[\converges.to{L}:for{S ::= a(n_)}]
States:
when:
. L is \real
. S is \real.sequence
that:
. forAll: epsilon is \real
  where: epsilon \:real.greater?:/ \real.zero
  then:
  . exists: N is \natural
    suchThat:
    . forAll: n is \natural
      where: N \:natural.leq?:/ n
      then: \real.abs(a(n) \.real.-./ L) \:real.less?:/ epsilon
Documented:
. called: "$S?$ converges to $L?$"
. written: "a?_{n_?} \to L?"
. description: "The sequence $a_n$ converges to limit $L$ as $n \to \infty$."
Id: "f046faf8-5c18-4597-ac14-4feda980148d"


[\(cauchy)::real.sequence]
Refines: S ::= a(n_)
specifies: S is \real.sequence
satisfies:
. forAll: epsilon is \real
  where: epsilon \:real.greater?:/ \real.zero
  then:
  . exists: N is \natural
    suchThat:
    . forAll: n, m is \natural
      where:
      . N \:natural.leq?:/ n
      . N \:natural.leq?:/ m
      then: \real.abs(a(n) \.real.-./ a(m)) \:real.less?:/ epsilon
Documented:
. adjective: "Cauchy"
. description: "A sequence is Cauchy if its terms eventually stay arbitrarily
                close to each other."
Id: "3bf9fa3d-791d-4ebf-b585-68dbdb2755b1"


[\(bounded)::real.sequence]
Refines: S ::= a(n_)
specifies: S is \real.sequence
satisfies:
. exists: M is \real
  suchThat:
  . forAll: n is \natural
    then: \real.abs(a(n)) \:real.leq?:/ M
Documented:
. adjective: "bounded"
. description: "A sequence is bounded if all of its values lie within a finite
                interval."
Id: "e2633f12-6e7f-401a-a4f1-d55bec7d279c"


[\(monotone.increasing)::real.sequence]
Refines: S ::= a(n_)
specifies: S is \real.sequence
satisfies:
. forAll: n is \natural
  then: a(n) \:real.leq?:/ a(n \.natural.+./ 1)
Documented:
. adjective: "monotone increasing"
. description: "A sequence is monotone increasing if each term is at least as
                large as the preceding term."
Id: "7316aa91-53ee-4313-b8d4-0bceb5001242"


SectionTitle: "Series and Completeness"
Id: "beec2879-0d3c-4393-acf2-01f8bf37ba09"


[\series.sum:of{S ::= a(n_)}]
Defines: s is \real
when: S is \real.sequence
Documented:
. called: "sum of series $S?$"
. written: "\sum_{n_?=1}^{\infty} a?_{n_?}"
. description: "The sum of the infinite series $\sum_{n=1}^\infty a_n$."
Id: "d9cbb77c-c12f-40ab-9a47-2e72f8efc719"


[\cauchy.completeness.theorem]
Theorem:
given: S ::= a(n_) is \real.sequence
then: S is? \(cauchy)::real.sequence
iff:
. exists: L is \real
  suchThat: \converges.to{L}:for{S}
Documented:
. called: "Cauchy Completeness of the Real Numbers"
. description: "In the real numbers, every Cauchy sequence converges to a limit."
Id: "da1c56ad-7de6-4161-b806-99ead8e954be"


[\monotone.convergence.theorem]
Theorem:
given: S ::= a(n_) is \real.sequence
where:
. S is \(monotone.increasing)::real.sequence
. S is \(bounded)::real.sequence
then:
. exists: L is \real
  suchThat: \converges.to{L}:for{S}
Documented:
. called: "Monotone Convergence Theorem"
. description: "Every bounded monotone real sequence converges."
Id: "3d7b0ef1-4562-415e-bf44-74e324ce5f5c"
